eedback. C has strong decision and attention, and crew cooperation. The concerns for C are communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Which is more critical? For long-distance pilot, safety-critical: decision quality, attention, crew cooperation are vital. Communication difficulty could be mitigated. Egocentric attitude could be problematic but maybe less than unknowns for B. So we might shift to C. We need to provide a public message referencing discussion, using explicit facts, and state recommendation for C.\n\nThus we will produce a public message: I now recommend Candidate C, because B lacks data on memory for numbers, adaptability, openness to feedback, while C has proven quick correct decisions, excellent attention, concern for others, which addresses decision quality, attention accuracy, crew cooperation. Acknowledge C's communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but those are less critical than unknowns for B. Also note that A and D have crew cooperation concerns. So we support C.\n\nNow output metadata with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
